{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Moses commanded, and they proclaimed throughout the camp</b> — The Torah was given on Shabbat, so Yom HaKippurim of that year was the third day, and on the fourth day he said to them [concerning] the work of the Tabernacle, and they brought it to him morning by morning, and that is the fifth day and the sixth day, and on Shabbat — \"and Moses commanded, and they proclaimed throughout the camp.\"" "<b>A man and a woman shall do no more work for the sacred contribution</b> — in gematria וזהו, and this is: they shall not take out the burden from the private domain to the public domain." "<b>ויכלא</b> — twice here, and the other one: ויכלא הגשם. This is what they expounded: precious stones and pearls used to come down for them with the manna, and they brought them to the Tabernacle donation. \"And the rain was restrained\" — i.e., the clouds that bring the rain — once they ceased bringing the precious stones, then the people ceased bringing."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:12.029952730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}